messages.content:
You are supporting a process mining research prototype.
Use only the synthetic scenario information provided below.
Do not invent company-specific system names, product names, confidential logs, internal metrics, or real organizational details.
Return valid JSON only. Do not wrap it in Markdown.

Scenario ID: C01
Scenario title: Morning Preparation and Childcare Drop-off
Initial workflow description:
I get my child ready in the morning, pack what we need, and take them to childcare. If we are running late, I let someone know.

Clarification questions:
[
  {
    "id": "Q1",
    "question": "What is the intended start time for the morning routine, and is it fixed each day or does it vary depending on the childcare schedule?"
  },
  {
    "id": "Q2",
    "question": "Can you walk me through the individual steps involved in getting your child ready, in the order they typically happen?"
  },
  {
    "id": "Q3",
    "question": "Does the set of items you pack change from day to day, and if so, what determines what needs to be included on a given day?"
  },
  {
    "id": "Q4",
    "question": "How do you determine that you are running late — is there a specific time threshold, a missed milestone in the routine, or something else?"
  },
  {
    "id": "Q5",
    "question": "When you notify someone that you are running late, who do you contact and through what channel — for example, a phone call, text message, or an app?"
  },
  {
    "id": "Q6",
    "question": "What actions do you need to complete at the childcare location during drop-off before you consider the process finished?"
  }
]
Reference workflow for oracle use:
{
  "goal": "Morning Preparation and Childcare Drop-off with explicit responsibilities, decisions and recorded completion.",
  "actors": [
    "mother",
    "partner",
    "childcare teacher",
    "backup caregiver"
  ],
  "systems": [
    "shared family calendar",
    "packing checklist",
    "childcare messaging app",
    "attendance register"
  ],
  "inputs": [
    "arrival window",
    "daily item list",
    "caregiver availability",
    "provider notice"
  ],
  "outputs": [
    "checked bag",
    "assigned escort",
    "arrival notice",
    "handover confirmation"
  ],
  "activities": [
    {
      "id": "A1",
      "name": "Check the arrival window and provider notice",
      "actor": "mother"
    },
    {
      "id": "A2",
      "name": "Confirm the escort with the partner",
      "actor": "mother"
    },
    {
      "id": "A3",
      "name": "Review the daily item list",
      "actor": "partner"
    },
    {
      "id": "A4",
      "name": "Pack and check the bag",
      "actor": "partner"
    },
    {
      "id": "A5",
      "name": "Resolve missing items before departure",
      "actor": "mother"
    },
    {
      "id": "A6",
      "name": "Escort the child to childcare",
      "actor": "mother"
    },
    {
      "id": "A7",
      "name": "Send an arrival delay notice when needed",
      "actor": "mother"
    },
    {
      "id": "A8",
      "name": "Confirm handover with the childcare teacher",
      "actor": "mother"
    }
  ],
  "decisions": [
    {
      "id": "D1",
      "condition": "Are all required items packed?",
      "branches": [
        "ready to depart",
        "check the agreed substitute or contact the teacher"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "D2",
      "condition": "Can the assigned escort meet the arrival window?",
      "branches": [
        "escort proceeds",
        "confirm the backup caregiver and notify the teacher"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "exceptions": [
    "missing required item",
    "escort unavailable",
    "arrival delay",
    "unacknowledged handover"
  ],
  "dependencies": [
    {
      "from": "A1",
      "to": "A2",
      "type": "control_flow"
    },
    {
      "from": "A2",
      "to": "A3",
      "type": "control_flow"
    },
    {
      "from": "A3",
      "to": "A4",
      "type": "control_flow"
    },
    {
      "from": "A4",
      "to": "A5",
      "type": "control_flow"
    },
    {
      "from": "A5",
      "to": "A6",
      "type": "control_flow"
    },
    {
      "from": "A6",
      "to": "A7",
      "type": "control_flow"
    },
    {
      "from": "A7",
      "to": "A8",
      "type": "control_flow"
    }
  ],
  "automation_opportunities": [
    {
      "target": "A1",
      "rationale": "Combine calendar reminders and provider notices for parent review."
    },
    {
      "target": "A4",
      "rationale": "Generate a dated packing checklist without confirming physical completion."
    },
    {
      "target": "A7",
      "rationale": "Draft delay messages for the parent's confirmation."
    }
  ],
  "operating_context": {
    "frequency": "weekday mornings",
    "manual_effort": "Checklist review and calendar coordination take about ten minutes in this fictional household.",
    "data_availability": "The calendar is shared with the partner; childcare messages remain in the provider app.",
    "integration_and_approval_constraints": "A reminder may be drafted automatically, but a parent confirms any escort change; handover remains in person."
  },
  "interpretation": "Activity dependencies describe the nominal sequence. Decision branches and exception descriptions qualify that sequence; this is not an executable BPMN model."
}
Task: Simulate a concise domain expert who answers only these questions using the reference workflow.
Do not reveal the full reference workflow. Do not add details not needed by the questions.
If a requested fact is absent, explicitly say it is not specified; do not guess.
Use at most 80 words per answer. Return one answer for each question, with matching ID and question text.
Return JSON: {"answers": [{"question_id": "Q1", "question": "original question", "answer": "grounded answer"}]}
